  "result": "The concept `drv.motion.stopping_distance` passed the gate with `OK` on the first run, so 5 of the 6 runs are left.\n\n**Body:** `kin_speed x * reaction_time + (kin_speed x)² / (2 * decel)`\n- **The literal 2:** I wrote the record's declared 2 as `Units.ratio 2 1` with the count unit tag, because `Units` has no count constructor.\n- **The divisor:** `2 * decel` reads no measured atom, which is what the language requires of a divisor, and the record states `decel` is strictly positive.\n- **Edge values:** a road user standing still gives 0, as the contract says, and the value is unknown when `kin.speed` is unobserved.\n\n**Witnesses:** one instance with a reaction time of 1 s, a deceleration of 5 m/s² and bounds of [19 m, 21 m]. Each trace has three observations, 1 s apart, of a car heading north at a steady speed.\n- **holds:** at 10 m/s the value is 10 + 100/10 = 20 m, inside the bounds.\n- **fails:** the same car at 20 m/s gives 20 + 400/10 = 60 m, so the bounds lie wholly below it. The scenarios share one instance and its bounds, so I had to change the speed here. That makes it the same road user at a different speed, not literally the same scene.\n- **blind:** the holds scene with `kin.speed` masked, which gives unknown.\n\nThe contract states the formula exactly, so I declared no narrowings. `task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
